cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QNM Analyser in your work, please cite it as given below."
title: "qnm-analyser: the quasinormal modes that agree across numerical resolutions"
abstract: >-
  QNM Analyser is an interactive web application, written in Python with Dash and Plotly, that
  tells genuine quasinormal modes from numerical noise in eigenvalues computed at several
  resolutions. It matches the roots of the highest resolution with those of the lower ones by
  nearest-neighbour search in KD-trees, keeps those that agree within a chosen tolerance,
  classifies them as general, purely imaginary or purely real, and draws and exports them.
type: software
